.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- extract zip archives with colon-path member mapping
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I zipfile
.RI [ member ]...
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path wrapper around
.BR unzip (1).
.PP
When a member is given as
.BR BASE:LEAF ,
archive members under the physical path
.B BASE/LEAF
are extracted and written to
.I LEAF
on disk.
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ a.zip a/b:/c/d/e
Extracts members
.B a/b/c/d/e/**
from
.B a.zip
and writes them to
.BR c/d/e/** .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Describe the extract/relocate plan without executing it.
.PP
Other options are passed through to
.BR unzip (1).
See the original manual for the complete option set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unzip (1),
.BR colon-zip (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
